+## Block-2 screen-4 v2 (avatar + fields + height) carry-forwards (2026-06-19)
+
+- **QA-002 systemic image-URL hardening — dedicated security pass.** `imageUrlSchema = z.string().url().nullable()` is the SHARED image-URL schema across 8+ usages (coach-profile selfUpdate, coach-athletes, coach-dashboard, iam/user, athlete). It accepts ANY url-shaped string → an attacker-controlled external URL persists + renders in privileged screens (coach roster / admin console). The ATHLETE write is now hardened (D-AV-IMAGE-BLOB-WRITE — `blobImageUrlSchema`), but the COACH selfUpdate write + the iam/user write paths are still permissive, and the shared READ schema stays permissive (so existing non-blob image data parses). Disposition: a dedicated pass — apply `blobImageUrlSchema` to all image WRITE paths (coach + user), add the length cap everywhere, audit/migrate existing non-blob `User.image` data, then tighten the READ schema. Moderate severity (no XSS/SSRF; stored attacker-URL → IP-leak/content-injection by an in-system user).
+- **gender → resolver wiring — profile-type-catalog wave (D-FIELDS-GENDER-INERT).** The typed `gender` field is INERT for load resolution (the resolver reads only free-string `profileSelections`; verified `load-records.ts` selects `{ weightKg, profileSelections }`, never `gender`). Wiring gender to drive a gendered byProfile axis needs the deferred profile-type catalog (typed axes, where a "sex/gender" axis type binds to the field) — a brittle axis-name convention is rejected. Until then gender is a stored attribute; gendered loads resolve via the free-string pick.
+- **Coach header avatar staleness — same latent bug, 1-liner.** The athlete avatar upload now calls `session.update({image})` so the header refreshes (D-AV-SESSION-UPDATE). The COACH upload (`coach-profile/sections/identity-hero-section.tsx`) does NOT — a coach's RE-uploaded avatar is stale in the header until re-login. Add the same `session.update` to the coach flow when convenient.
+- **api-server `image` get/upsert assertions — GATED, write on a gated run.** The `athlete-profile.test.ts` get-join + upsert-split image assertions (+ transaction-rollback / non-image-update-leaves-image cases) were NOT written (the api-server suite is a ~10-min gated live-Neon run). check-types + the platform integration cover the shape; add the gated assertions on the next approved api-server run.
+- **`isBlobStorageUrl` duplication — dedupe on a 3rd consumer.** The blob-host predicate now lives in both `common/image.ts` (`blobImageUrlSchema`) and `storage/upload/upload-api.schema.ts` (`deleteImageRequestSchema`). Two consumers, different schema shapes; on a 3rd, lift the predicate to one shared spot.
